PULSE ANALYTICS – PHASE 2 BUSINESS REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT (BRD)

1.Executive Summary
Pulse Phase 2 expands the Gold Standard benchmarking framework built in Phase 1 into a decision-intelligence platform enabling four high-value manufacturing capabilities:
1.Overfill Optimization 
2.Gap Cover-Intelligence Insights
3.New Product Launch (NPL) Predictive Performance
4.Dynamic Short-Term Scheduling (Sequencing)

These capabilities unlock significant operational value by reducing material losses, improving throughput efficiency, enhancing planning accuracy for new products, and enabling smarter daily production decisions.

Phase 2 is built on the enterprise data (EDL, RDL, SAP, PDS, TML, Pack Assist, LIMS, QA-(LIMS, Free Weigh, Veeva Quality One), OT) and extends the Gold Standard logic into predictive and prescriptive use cases.

This BRD defines all functional, data, integration, and non-functional requirements that vendors must adhere to. It establishes clear feasibility boundaries and expectations to ensure realistic delivery.
2. Business Objectives
2.1 Overfill Optimization

Reduce overfill giveaway through accurate/standardized measurement, identification of root-cause drivers, modeling of historical performance, and forecasting of overfill risks by SKU, line, shift, package, and component MASS. 
SKU × Line × Shift × Day 
The solution will quantify financial impact and provide advisory recommendations to reduce material giveaway while maintaining regulatory compliance and aesthetic standards.

2.2 Gap Cover Intelligent Insights
The Gap Cover Intelligent Insights module extends the Gold Standard framework established in Phase 1 by operationalizing continuous performance gap detection and prioritized improvement recommendations. 
This module should identify the performance gaps between:
Legacy SKUs vs Gold Standard SKUs
Lines vs optimal asset performance
Shifts/operators vs benchmark levels
Actual vs theoretical performance (GS speed, scrap, labor, overfill)
Enable ongoing optimization of manufacturing performance by:
Detecting underperforming SKUs relative to Gold Standard
Quantifying cost-of-gap at SKU × Line × Shift level
Prioritizing opportunities by financial impact
Providing short-term operational recommendations
Identifying long-term structural improvement opportunities
The system converts these gaps into quantified, actionable improvement opportunities tied directly to financial impact.
Performance Gap Types
The system must calculate the following gap categories:
OEE Gap
 GS_OEE – Actual_OEE
Speed Gap
  GS_Speed – Actual_Speed
Scrap Gap
  Actual_Scrap% – GS_Scrap%
Overfill Gap
 Actual_Overfill% – GS_Overfill_Target
Labor Efficiency Gap
  Actual_Labor_Hours – GS_Labor_Standard
 Actual_Crew_Size – GS__Crew _Size_Recommend
Financial Impact Calculation
Each performance gap must be translated into financial value:(USD across all regions)
OEE Gap → Throughput opportunity
Scrap Gap → Scrap cost delta
Overfill Gap → Giveaway cost
Labor Gap → Excess labor cost
Total Gap Cost per SKU =
 (OEE loss impact + Scrap cost delta + Overfill cost delta + Labor delta)
The system must rank SKUs by total financial gap impact.


2.3 Predictive New Product Launch (NPL) Performance

Model expected performance of new products (scrap %, line speed, OEE, overfill risk, changeover time) by comparing SKU attributes against historical launches.
The goal is to:
Improve vertical startup success 
Predict operational risk before launch
Recommend optimal line allocation
Reduce post-launch stabilization time
Align new SKUs to Gold Standard performance targets
Predictions must include:
Scrap %
Line speed
OEE
Overfill risk
Changeover time
PO Size


2.4 Dynamic Short-Term Scheduling

Objective
Enable optimized daily and shift-level production sequencing for Fill & Assembly lines to:
Reduce changeover losses
Maximize throughput
Improve adherence to Gold Standard performance
Increase asset utilization
Provide quantified decision support to production planners
The system will generate optimized sequence recommendations and simulate expected performance impact prior to execution.
Purpose
Develop a deterministic sequencing optimization engine that:
Evaluates multiple SKU order permutations
Minimizes total changeover time
Maximizes expected throughput
Aligns production performance with Gold Standard benchmarks
Provides scenario comparison capability
The engine will operate at a single-line level per shift/day for Phase 2.
