4. AS-IS Challenges Driving Phase 2

4.1 Overfill Challenges

Current limitations include:
High variability across lines, shifts, and operators
Package/format-driven mass differences not modeled
Specific Gravity (SG) variations inconsistently applied
No standardized tolerance windows across plants
Manual overfill measurement processes
Scrap and mass variance not unified into one logic
No predictive visibility into overfill risk
Limited root-cause attribution (operator vs filler vs packaging vs formulation)
These gaps result in significant giveaway exposure ($25–40M annually).

4.2 NPL Challenges 

Challenges with Vertical start up for NPL to meet Gold Standard:
No structured benchmark for predicting NPL performance
Packaging complexity not mapped to historical line capability
BOM and changeover complexity not quantified
No system to simulate expected through put, scrap, OEE, or overfill for upcoming launches


4.3 Sequencing Challenges

Manual scheduling based on heuristics
No quantified view of changeover penalties
No dynamic sequence based on resource capability 
Lack of real-time link between line capability, SKU attributes, and GS benchmarks
No simulation environment for “What if we change the sequence?”
No linkage between sequencing and Gold Standard benchmarks
Limited visibility into financial impact of sequence decisions

These gaps justify the development of an advanced, analytics-driven Phase 2 solution.

