5.4 Unified Gold Standard Extensions

All Phase 2 outputs align back to:
• GS speed benchmarks
• GS scrap benchmarks
 • GS Labor Utilization
 • GS OEE Performance

6. MODULE 1 – Overfill Optimization Requirements                                                                                                                           6.1 Purpose

Create a standardized, predictive overfill optimization solution that reduces giveaway, aligns fill performance to GS QPA benchmarks, and identifies operational, material, and equipment drivers.
Develop a standardized overfill calculation and predictive risk solution that:
Normalizes mass using SG
Aligns fill performance to GS benchmarks
Identifies operational and material drivers
Quantifies financial giveaway
Enables structured tolerance management
6.2 Key Overfill Formulas

6.2.1 Core Formulas
 Overfill vs legal:  QPA – legal claim
QPA - legal claim + 1 ml 

Target Fill Volume =Claim volume + regulatory & aesthetic requirements = Lower spec limit (LSL) in PDS
Target fill volume = LSL + 3 x variance of the filler
Overfill Quantity = Actual Fill Quantity - claimed quantity (claim that is on the package x avg SG)
1. Regulatory & aestheic requirements=LSL-Claim
Filler variance =target – LSL Lower spec limit 
Set-up = actual fill - target fill
QPA variance = QPA - fill target x SG

Overfill % = (Actual – Target) / Target × 100

Giveaway Cost = Overfill Quantity × Material Unit Cost
 
6.2.2 Specific Gravity Adjustment
 
Convert Target Volume to Target Weight
Target Fill Weight = Target Fill Volume × SG
Calculate Overfill in Weight
Overfill Weight = Actual Weight – Target Fill Weight
Actual Fill Volume = Actual Weight ÷ SG
Overfill Volume = Actual Fill Volume – Target Fill Volume
Cost:
 Overfill Weight = Overfill Volume × SG

Adjusted Fill Weight = Actual Weight / SG
Overfill (Adj) = Adjusted Fill Weight – Target Fill Weight
  

6.2.3 Statistical Control
 
Control Limits =Target fill +/- 3 sigma give LCL & UCL

